    <comment>NEW PACKAGE (supersedes sr#1372083): Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires, matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck does not demand a non-ring package.

- Convert the Python binding to the shared loader:
  * Drop %treesitter_python_build; keep
    %treesitter_python_install only
  * Generated _binding.py loads the grammar library this
    package ships, so the parser is not compiled a second
    time
  * Drop python devel/installer/pip/setuptools/wheel
    BuildRequires; keep python-rpm-macros, fdupes and
    %{python_module base}
  * Pin python-%{name} to %{name} = %{version}-%{release}
- Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package
- Run a functional %check parsing Swift source through the
  shim; gated to suse_version &gt;= 1699 because
  python-tree-sitter does not exist in Leap 16.0

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together:
 * sr#1372054 - tree-sitter (python binding macros)
 * sibling new-grammar SRs from editors:tree-sitter
Needed for python-graphifyy.</comment>
